cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Testosterone raises PSA, and much of its apparent prostate cancer risk runs through that channel: a Mendelian randomization and Bayesian synthesis study"
abstract: >-
  A Mendelian randomization and Bayesian evidence synthesis study. Using PSA as
  an in vivo bioassay of prostatic androgen receptor signaling, it falsifies the
  androgen saturation model, excludes reverse causation and metabolic
  confounding, identifies a PSA driven detection signature across exposures and
  cohorts, and shows that randomized trials of testosterone therapy double
  prostate biopsies without increasing prostate cancer.
